g through 2027.\n  - Utilities are growing faster than data centres.\n  - Pellham Power plans 2027 capex up 18%, including a transformer tender of about C$900M due to award in Q1 2027.\n  - Data-centre connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027, slower than in 2026.\n  - VLTX's utility order intake was C$670M in 2026Q3.\n- **Financing is a risk to that demand.** Utilities probably can't count on equity markets, and debt is available but getting more expensive.\n  - Equity looks largely shut: two utility share offerings were cut back in size in Q3.\n  - Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp, so debt is open but costlier.\n  - Nobody sized the 2027 funding gap, so I can't say how much of the planned capex is at risk of being delayed or cut.\n- **Pricing gives no edge.** VLTX LEAPS look fairly priced: implied volatility is 27%, against a 2-year median of 26%. The Jan-2029 implied volatility is 27.5%. They aren't cheap, so you'd be paying a full price for the upside.\n\nThe demand thesis supports owning the LEAPS, but the pricing is neutral and the funding risk is unresolved. That doesn't justify a larger bet right now.\n\nTwo things would change my view. One is evidence on the size of the funding gap, or a Q1 2027 award that goes ahead on schedule. The other is a dip in implied volatility below its median, which would make adding cheaper.\n\nFull detail is in n2.r1, n3.r1 and n4.r1.","ttft_ms":2500,"type":"result","duration_ms":51763,"uuid":"2da1f56d-2fb0-49df-983b-87c9d6c931f4","ttft_stream_ms":1510,"time_to_request_ms":471,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":50,"system_prompt":45,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":97,"input_hooks":11,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":27,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":36,"init_frame_send":15,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":28,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":4,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":48,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":26,"tool_schema_build":22,"message_nor